; bml-recover-surface-band.fk — BML's own words for the recover point and for absence.
;
; `try e else h` attempts e; when e stops (a length of nothing, a branch on nothing)
; or answers nothing, h answers. `choose { e1; e2; ... }` attempts each option in
; order; the first that lands wins and none landing is nothing. `x ?? y` is x unless
; x is nothing. All three lower to (attempt ...) and nothing? with the next option in
; the if's branch, so an option that is not needed is never walked.
;
; Verdict 1023 when every claim lands:
;   1     try recovers a stop: the length of nothing reads the else, 7
;   2     try passes a value that landed: a two-element list reads 2
;   4     choose walks past two stopping options to its third, 99
;   8     choose takes its first landing option: the bytes of "abcd", 4
;   16    ?? fills nothing, 5
;   32    ?? keeps a value that arrived, 9
;   64    a stop in an inner try's else unwinds to the outer try, 11
;   128   an else that is not needed is never walked: 3, where walking it would stop
;   256   a choose whose every option declines answers nothing
;   512   try inside a block let: the frame stands after the recovery, 0 + 1
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/tests/bml-recover-surface-fixture.bml

(do
    (defn rsb-bit (ok v) (if ok v 0))
    (add (rsb-bit (eq (rs-len (nothing)) 7) 1)
    (add (rsb-bit (eq (rs-len (list 1 2)) 2) 2)
    (add (rsb-bit (eq (rs-first (nothing)) 99) 4)
    (add (rsb-bit (eq (rs-first "abcd") 4) 8)
    (add (rsb-bit (eq (rs-or (nothing)) 5) 16)
    (add (rsb-bit (eq (rs-or 9) 9) 32)
    (add (rsb-bit (eq (rs-nested (nothing)) 11) 64)
    (add (rsb-bit (eq (rs-lazy) 3) 128)
    (add (rsb-bit (nothing? (rs-none)) 256)
         (rsb-bit (eq (rs-block (nothing)) 1) 512)))))))))))
